' DO ... LOOP in its five forms. After a DO without a condition, LOOP starts a new line unless the
' body is empty (zxbc's grammar; parser error E315), so the bottom-tested forms take two lines
'@expect screen 0 "3 3 1 1 3 0"
DIM i AS UByte
i = 0: DO WHILE i < 3: i = i + 1: LOOP: PRINT i; " ";
i = 0: DO UNTIL i = 3: i = i + 1: LOOP: PRINT i; " ";
i = 0: DO: i = i + 1
LOOP WHILE i > 5: PRINT i; " ";
i = 0: DO: i = i + 1
LOOP UNTIL i > 0: PRINT i; " ";
i = 0: DO: i = i + 1: IF i = 3 THEN EXIT DO
LOOP
PRINT i; " ";
i = 0: DO LOOP UNTIL i = 0: PRINT i
